LOCAL PATCH (2026-11-20, KaChat-Desktop, the kUSDT port)
  kusdt/kusdt_wasm.js, two changes; the .wasm is unchanged:
  1. __wbg_newnoargs answers "return this" with a function returning globalThis, and workflow-core's
     promise-with-resolvers helper ("let resolve, reject; const p = new Promise(...); p.resolve =
     resolve; p.reject = reject; return p;", compared with whitespace collapsed) with a plain
     function, instead of `new Function(...)` - the same patch as kaspa/kaspa.js Builds 134 and 145.
     The app's CSP (tools/security-headers.mjs, public/_headers) has no 'unsafe-eval'. Those are the
     only two snippets kusdt_wasm_bg.wasm holds (searched 2026-11-20; it has no requestAnimationFrame
     fallback, unlike kaspa_bg.wasm, Build 148); anything else still goes to Function and the CSP
     refuses it.
  2. __wbg_init without a module throws instead of fetching new URL('kusdt_wasm_bg.wasm',
     import.meta.url): the bytes always come from engine/kusdt-core.js, checked against the pin
     first, so an unchecked .wasm can never load through the loader (and Vite doesn't emit a second
     copy of it).
  After an INTENTIONAL change to these files: bash tools/check-wasm.sh --update, and update this file.
